    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33196" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ŏtācĭlĭus</span></b> ,
		i, m., <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ŏtācĭlĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the name of a Roman</i> gens. So,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> Otacilius Crassus, <i>an adherent of Pompey</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B.
				C. 3, 28 sq.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> T. Otacilius, <i>a proprœtor</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Liv.
				22, 56</span></i>.—In <i>fem.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">OTACILIA,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut. 29, 2</span></i>
			; Eckh. D. N. 7, p. 332.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> OTACILIANA VILLA, <i>of
				an Otacilius</i>, Inscr. Marin. Fratr. Arv. p. 577.</div>
